-- Step 2 of 2: point every catalogue caption and blurb at its key.
--
-- Run catalog-page-slug-repair.sql FIRST. This file was generated against the slugs that script
-- produces, so without it 100 pages point at keys that do not exist -- and a missing key resolves
-- to the empty string, so those pages go blank rather than failing.
--
-- The keys live in gamedata/external_catalog_text.json, in Habbo's own shape: catalog.page.<slug>
-- for the caption, .text_<n> for a blurb. The client resolves a caption only when it reads
-- `${key}`; TextLabelController tests charAt(0) and charAt(1) and nothing else, which is why the
-- bare slugs these columns held until now were displayed verbatim.
--
-- The asset host must be serving that file before this runs, and the client must be a build that
-- follows the external_text_* entries in the manifest. Neither is checked here: run this last.
--
-- Generated by tools/catalog_converter/extract_catalog_texts.py.
-- Re-runnable: absolute values, so a second run leaves the same rows.
--
